Case 
     D NUM             S              1I 0

     C                   EVAL      NUM = 2

     C                   SELECT
     C     NUM           WHENEQ    1
     C                   DSPLY     'ONE'

     C     NUM           WHENEQ    2
     C                   DSPLY     'TWO'

     C                   OTHER
     C                   DSPLY     'OTHER'

     C                   ENDSL

     C                   SETON                                        LR


Loop

     D I               S              3I 0

     C                   EVAL      I = 1

     C     I             DOWLE     5

     C                   DSPLY     I

     C                   ADD       1             I

     C                   ENDDO

     C                   SETON                                        LR

If

     D NUM             S              3I 0

     C                   EVAL      NUM = 10

     C     NUM           IFGT      5
     C                   DSPLY     'BIG'
     C                   ENDIF

     C                   SETON                                        LR

Declare a file 

     FCUSTOMER  IF   E           K DISK
Meaning:

	• F = file spec
	• CUSTOMER = file name
	• I = input
	• F = full procedural
	• E = externally described
	• K = keyed
	• DISK = database file

Typical non-keyed sequential file:

     FSALES     IF   E             DISK



Read a file 

     FCUSTOMER  IF   E             DISK

     C                   READ      CUSTOMER
     C                   DOW       NOT %EOF(CUSTOMER)

     C                   DSPLY     CUSNAME

     C                   READ      CUSTOMER

     C                   ENDDO

     C                   SETON                                        LR


Write a file 

     FCUSTOMER  O    E             DISK

     C                   EVAL      CUSNO = 1001
     C                   EVAL      CUSNAME = 'NICK'

     C                   WRITE     CUSTOMER

     C                   SETON                                        LR




